_64-unknown-linux-gnu-debug.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"epic-lore-bot[bot]","id":289003844,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOETnZRA","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":124333531,"digest":"sha256:ed23f991d0f449bfbd0aeeea88a7ee7baab39d62fd6d7387ce87ca23b2c54191","download_count":7,"created_at":"2026-11-12T16:33:14Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T16:33:18Z"},{"id":740213866,"node_id":"RA_kwDOSkSdJs4sHsRq","name":"loreserver-v0.14.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"epic-lore-bot[bot]","id":289003844,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOETnZRA","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":18565762,"digest":"sha256:900c0b508d2bb8856d9de1824c457b10bd3b33c1e0927fdecd9ed8511446cf81","download_count":357,"created_at":"2026-11-12T16:33:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T16:33:20Z"}],"body":"The latest release of Lore, Epic Games' next-generation open source version control system.\r\n\r\n[Quickstart](https://epicgames.github.io/lore/tutorials/quickstart/) | [Design](https://epicgames.github.io/lore/explanation/system-design/) | [Documentation](https://epicgames.github.io/lore/) | [Discord](https://discord.gg/E4SFJKRPbg)\r\n\r\n## Quick Install\r\n\r\nWindows\r\n```\r\nirm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EpicGames/lore/main/scripts/install.ps1 | iex\r\n```\r\n\r\nmacOS / Linux\r\n```\r\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EpicGames/lore/main/scripts/install.sh | bash\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Release Notes\r\n\r\nChanges since v0.13.0.\r\n\r\n### Breaking changes\r\n\r\n* Branch metadata keys `archived`, `restored`, `restoring` and `released` are reserved for archives and restores; remove or rename values stored under them before upgrading\r\n* An invalid `LORE_AUTH_STORE`, or a user-level `config.toml` that can't be read or parsed, stops every command. Commands relayed to the service without `LORE_AUTH_STORE` use the secure store\r\n* The Lore service and its clients must come from the same build; end a running service after upgrading\r\n* Requests the server or authentication service refuses fail with `NotAuthenticated` (16) or `NotAuthorized` (17) instead of an internal error (255), `NotConnected` (29) or a not-found code\r\n* `lore branch create` with an invalid name and a refused `lore repository instance move` exit with `InvalidArguments` (3); `lore clone --root-file` with a missing file exits with 82\r\n* C API: push events start with their `repository` and `branch`, and the instance-delete begin event drops `dry_run`. Rebuild against the new `lore.h`\r\n* Switching, resetting or pushing to an archived branch leaves it archived; `lore push` restores it, other clients restore it with a branch create\r\n* Mutable store plugins must remove a key swapped to zero and refuse a swap from a non-zero value on an absent key\r\n* `lore-server`: a `remote` immutable store trusts its upstream and checks only payload sizes (`verify = true` restores full checks)\r\n* `lore-server`: QUIC storage request failures log under the `lore_server::quic` target\r\n\r\n### Features\r\n\r\n* Virtual clones on Linux with `lore clone --vfs fuse`, served from the shared store and supporting status, stage, commit, sync, reset and merge. `--vfs default` now picks FUSE on Linux\r\n* `lore clone --vfs fuse --prefetch <file>` warms the store from an access recording (`LORE_FUSE_RECORD_DIR`)\r\n* `lore repository instance clone` copies an instance on a shared store, sharing data blocks on APFS, Btrfs, XFS, ReFS and Dev Drive\r\n* `[auth]` in the user-level `config.toml` chooses the token store (`store`, `path`)\r\n* Per-instance ignore rules in `.lore/ignore`\r\n* `--fast-flush` writes the local store's index in place, which is faster on Windows\r\n* `[store] cache_payloads` sets whether fetched and written content is kept in the store\r\n* The Lore service closes remote connections idle for 5 minutes (`idle_connection_timeout`)\r\n* `lore-unix://` remotes reach a machine server through a Unix socket (`LORE_UDS_SOCKET`), which `lore-server` serves to containers with `[server.uds]`\r\n* `lore-server`: `client_credentials_scopes` for OIDC providers, requested by `lore auth login --client-id`\r\n* `lore-server`: round-robin read replica selection for composite stores (`read_replica_selection`)\r\n* `lore-server`: HTTP range requests on the content and presigned endpoints\r\n* `lore-server`: `ThinClientService.RevisionTree` can attribute entries to the revision that last changed them\r\n* `lore-server`: `server.upstream_connections` sets the connections to a `remote` store's upstream (default 4)\r\n\r\n### Fixes & Improvements\r\n\r\n* `lore push` pushes branches, layers and links up to 8 at a time, and each linked branch only once\r\n* Faster lookup of the revision shared with the remote, without endless loops or wrong merge bases\r\n* Fixed concurrent branch creates, restores, archives and metadata edits undoing each other\r\n* Merges, cherry-picks, reverts and syncs handle case-only renames on both sides\r\n* Fixed `lore file dirty`, `lore file dirty move` and `lore stage move` losing moves or dropping files from a commit\r\n* Fixed forced stages, unstages and merges under a sparse view corrupting or losing changes\r\n* Replacing a file with a folder, or the reverse, reports a merge conflict instead of failing with `Not a directory`\r\n* Fixed several merge, resolve, reset and obliterate problems inside links\r\n* Instances on a shared store keep their file times in `.lore/records/`, so they no longer rewrite each other's\r\n* Commands that change the user-level `config.toml` keep settings they don't know\r\n* Fixed content missing from the local store after concurrent reads or eviction, and commits failing with \"leader upload failed\"\r\n* C API revision-tree handles are safe under concurrent deletes and moves\r\n* SWFS: release builds need no dynamic C runtime, and files a sync brings back are no longer missing\r\n* `lore-server`: fixed `lore push --fast-forward-merge` storing revisions with mismatched directory hashes\r\n* `lore-server`: DynamoDB compare-and-swap fixes for zero values and refused swaps\r\n* `lore-server`: the replicated immutable store spreads requests over several connections (`num_clients`)\r\n* `lore-server`: fixed `RevisionDiff` and `RevisionTree` results around links and merges\r\n* `lore-server`: accepts partition-scoped tokens from a separate `token_exchange_issuer`\r\n\r\n## Release Assets\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]\r\nThese can be downloaded under the \"Assets\" section below.\r\n\r\n### Installer\r\n- `lore-setup` - Lore CLI Windows installer\r\n\r\n### Binaries\r\n- `lore` - Lore CLI\r\n- `loreserver` - Lore Server\r\n- `liblore` - Lore Shared Library\r\n\r\n### Headers\r\n- `lore.h` - Single header for `liblore` (packaged with `liblore`)\r\n\r\n### Supported Platforms\r\n- Windows x86_64\r\n- macOS AArch64\r\n- Linux x86_64\r\n- Linux AArch64\r\n- Linux AArch64, optimized for Graviton/Neoverse 512-tvb\r\n\r\n## Lore Desktop Client\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]\r\nLore Desktop Client is available as binaries only, download the installer for your platform here:\r\n\r\n- Windows: [Lore-Desktop-Setup-x64.exe](https://releases.lore.org/desktop/releases/stable/Lore-Desktop-Setup-x64.exe)\r\n- macOS: [Lore-Desktop-arm64.dmg](https://releases.lore.org/desktop/releases/stable/Lore-Desktop-arm64.dmg)\r\n- Linux (Ubuntu 24.04): [lore-desktop_amd64.deb](https://releases.lore.org/desktop/releases/stable/lore-desktop_amd64.deb)\r\n- Linux (AppImage): [Lore-Desktop-x86_64.AppImage](https://releases.lore.org/desktop/releases/stable/Lore-Desktop-x86_64.AppImage)\r\n\r\n##  ⬇️ Open Source Lore Assets Below ⬇️","reactions":{"total_count":22,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":5,"confused":0,"heart":4,"rocket":5,"eyes":0}}
